      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Understanding Python Comments"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's look at another example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1# Print a number \n2print(6)\n3print(8)  # Print another number \n4# Print third number \n5print(88.3)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This code has three comments:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "# Print a number \n# Print another number \n# Print third number"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Python skips all of them when running the program. Only the print() lines are executed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So this is the same as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1print(6)\n2print(8)\n3print(88.3)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The output will be:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "6\n8\n88.3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The comments help explain the code, but do not affect what the program does."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
